      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On perusal of Spot sketch and Charge sheet it appears that, near Mylapura Gate Hosakote,\nopposite to NH - 75 Hotel, Bangalore driver of 11 SCCH - 19 MVC.7057/2022 KSRTC bus bearing Reg. No.KA-57/F-3773 drove the same in a rash and negligent"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "675003dd2d474a05812b1a0e1dc380e9_77",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The said Lorry which was Ramesh vs K.S.R.T.C on 20 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199618399/\n5 parked on the road by its driver without any precautionary measures."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "82b8ad402e5b43edb50d271732189efd_78",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Further IMV report discloses that, the rear portion of the Lorry and front portion of the KSRTC bus were damaged."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "eee9a37423b8483aa67c8eefb1fc78e7_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Hence,\nHosakote Police filed Charge sheet against driver of the KSRTC Bus as A1 and driver of Lorry as A2."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8309b3843d464a069cd1ebc03e736600_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n22 . In the petition for compensation U/Sec.166 of Motor Vehicles Act.1988 the claimant has to prove the incident only on the preponderance of the probabilities and standard of proof beyond all reasonable doubt is not required as held by t"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a7fcb4b394544c9eb4c9b0f7ad6e62d6_81",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe so-called reason that as the name of Dheeraj Kumar was not mentioned in the FIR, so it was not possible for Dheeraj Kumar to see the incident, is not a proper assessment of the fact-situation in this case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1eb632152ca64c65b6ffba87ffc06ac8_82",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is well known that in a case relating to motor accident claims, the claimants are not required to prove the case as it is required to be done in a criminal trial."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "81ea70180c304e0280dbf05e6267ad33_83",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Court must keep this distinction in mind."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b4733900d27f471b93cf7bdbe7f1734a_84",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n12 SCCH - 19 MVC.7057/2022 10."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5a1063f131df4b1bab151778bca106e1_85",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Reference in this connection may be made to the decision of this Court in Bimla Devi and others V/s Himachal Road Transport Corporation and others (2009) 13 SCC 530, in which the relevant observation on this point has been made and which is"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "67073d9780d946548453a52bae2cf33c_86",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was necessary to be borne in mind that strict proof of an accident caused by a particular bus in a particular manner may not be possible to be done by the claimants."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "59c229805a834410a56078a6070d7827_87",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The claimants were merely to establish their case on the touch stone of preponderance of probability."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f2cd0617445d4c62904e69770806c46e_88",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The standard of proof beyond reasonable doubt could not have been applied.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f9996a825fac49fbb4e3843e922f37b0_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
